<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Nov 11.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Nov 11.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>International prices for milling wheat were firmer with support coming from lack of activity, the Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said. Wheat indicator prices for multi-grade contracts for 1996/97 crop wheat rose A$1.00 (Duram prices not applicable). Prices, FOB, in A$/tonne:</p>
<p>		    ASW 10 pct		   No 1 DURUM</p>
<p>		    Delivered Port	     Delivered Port</p>
<p>Queensland</p>
<p>    Brisbane	n/a</p>
<p>    Gladstone     n/a</p>
<p>    Mackay	  n/a</p>
<p>New South Wales</p>
<p>    Newcastle     121.75			   n/a</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   128.75</p>
<p>Victoria</p>
<p>    Geelong	 129.00</p>
<p>    Portland	129.75</p>
<p>South Australia</p>
<p>    Port Adelaide 129.75			   n/a</p>
<p>    Port Giles    130.50</p>
<p>Port Lincoln  132.00</p>
<p>    Port Pirie    126.50</p>
<p>    Thevenard     127.00</p>
<p>    Wallaroo	128.25</p>
<p>Western Australia</p>
<p>    Albany	  135.25</p>
<p>    Esperance     133.75</p>
<p>    Fremantle     138.00</p>
<p>    Geraldton     135.00</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1996/97 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Summer Time (0530 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
